The Security Council,
Recalling all its relevant resolutions, including resolutions 2118 (2013), 2209 (2015), 2235 (2015), 2254 (2015), 2258 (2015), 2286 (2016), 2314 (2016), 2319 (2016), 2328 (2016), 2330 (2016), 2332 (2016) and 2342 (2017),
Reaffirming its strong commitment to the sovereignty, independence, unity and territorial integrity of the Syrian Arab Republic,
Reaffirming the prohibition of the use of chemical weapons under the Convention on the Prohibition of the Development, Production, Stockpiling and Use of Chemical Weapons and on Their Destruction (the Convention), and recalling that any use of chemical weapons constitutes a serious violation of international law,
Recalling the obligations of the Syrian Arab Republic under resolution 2118 (2013) and the Convention, including the requirement to cooperate fully with the Organisation for the Prohibition of Chemical Weapons (OPCW),
Expressing grave concern at the reports of chemical weapons use in Khan Shaykhun, Idlib Governorate, on 4 April 2017, and at the loss of civilian life,
Condemning the use of chemical weapons by any party in the Syrian Arab Republic and stressing that those responsible for any such use must be held accountable,
Welcoming the decision of the OPCW to investigate the reports of chemical weapons use in Khan Shaykhun, and recalling the establishment of the OPCW-United Nations Joint Investigative Mechanism (JIM),
Stressing the need for all parties to cooperate fully with the OPCW and the JIM and to provide immediate, safe and unhindered access to all relevant sites and information,
Deeply concerned by the continuing suffering of the civilian population in Syria and recalling the need for all parties to comply with international humanitarian law,
Emphasizing the importance of a swift and impartial investigation in order to establish the facts and to ensure accountability,
Noting that the use of chemical weapons poses a threat to international peace and security,
1. Condemns the use of chemical weapons in the Syrian Arab Republic, including the reported attack in Khan Shaykhun on 4 April 2017, and expresses its outrage at the loss of civilian life;
2. Reaffirms that any use of chemical weapons constitutes a serious violation of international law and a threat to international peace and security;
3. Demands that all parties refrain from any use of chemical weapons and comply with their obligations under the Convention and relevant Security Council resolutions;
4. Calls upon the Syrian Arab Republic to cooperate fully with the OPCW and the JIM, including by providing immediate, safe and unhindered access to all relevant sites and by making available all relevant information, as requested;
5. Calls upon all other parties to the conflict to cooperate fully with the OPCW and the JIM and to ensure the safety and security of their personnel;
6. Requests the Director-General of the OPCW to report to the Security Council on the progress and outcome of the investigation into the Khan Shaykhun incident within 30 days, and to keep the Council regularly informed;
7. Requests the JIM to investigate the Khan Shaykhun incident and to report to the Security Council within 90 days;
8. Calls upon all Member States to support the investigation, including by sharing relevant information with the OPCW and the JIM;
9. Stresses the importance of preserving evidence and ensuring accountability for those responsible for the use of chemical weapons in the Syrian Arab Republic;
10. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

The Security Council,
Recalling all its relevant resolutions, including resolutions 2118 (2013), 2209 (2015), 2235 (2015), 2254 (2015), 2258 (2015), 2286 (2016), 2314 (2016), 2319 (2016), 2328 (2016), 2330 (2016), 2332 (2016) and 2342 (2017),
