Deeply concerned by the continuing suffering of the civilian population in Syria and recalling the need for all parties to comply with international humanitarian law,
Emphasizing the importance of a swift and impartial investigation in order to establish the facts, identify those responsible and ensure accountability,
Noting that the use of chemical weapons poses a threat to international peace and security,
1. Condemns in the strongest terms the chemical weapons attack in Khan Shaykhun on 4 April 2017, and expresses its outrage at the loss of civilian life;
2. Reaffirms that any use of chemical weapons constitutes a serious violation of international law and a threat to international peace and security;
3. Reaffirms the sovereignty, independence, unity and territorial integrity of the Syrian Arab Republic, and calls upon all States to refrain from any action that could further escalate tensions in the region;
4. Demands that all parties refrain from any use of chemical weapons and comply with their obligations under the Convention and relevant Security Council resolutions;
5. Demands that the Syrian Arab Republic, as required by resolution 2118 (2013) and the Convention, provide the OPCW and the JIM with immediate, safe and unhindered access to all relevant sites, including Shayrat airbase, and make available all relevant information, including flight plans, flight logs and records of air operations on 4 April 2017, and to ensure the safety and security of OPCW and JIM personnel;
6. Calls upon all other parties to the conflict, including armed groups and terrorist organizations, to cooperate fully with the OPCW and the JIM and to ensure the safety and security of their personnel and safe, immediate and unhindered access;
7. Demands that all parties allow immediate, safe and unhindered humanitarian access throughout Syria, and respect and protect medical and humanitarian personnel, consistent with resolutions 2258 (2015) and 2286 (2016);
8. Requests the Director-General of the OPCW to report to the Security Council on the progress and outcome of the investigation into the Khan Shaykhun incident within 30 days, and to keep the Council regularly informed;
9. Requests the JIM to investigate the Khan Shaykhun incident in an impartial, transparent and independent manner and to report to the Security Council within 90 days;
10. Calls upon all Member States to support the investigation, including by sharing relevant information with the OPCW and the JIM;
11. Stresses the importance of preserving evidence and ensuring accountability for those responsible for the use of chemical weapons in the Syrian Arab Republic, as determined by the OPCW and the JIM in accordance with international law, and affirms that the JIM's findings should be followed by appropriate action by the Security Council;
12. Expresses its intention to consider further measures, including sanctions, in the event of non-compliance with this resolution by any party, in particular the Syrian Arab Republic;
13. Reaffirms that a political solution is the only sustainable way to end the conflict and calls for the resumption of intra-Syrian negotiations under United Nations auspices in accordance with resolution 2254 (2015);
14. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

